<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bakhchysarai</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Bakhchisaray</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bakhchysarai is a town in the south-west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimea">Crimean peninsula</a>. It was the capital of the Crimean Khanate from the 16th century until the Russian annexation of 1783, and its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bakhchysarai-palace">Khan's Palace</a>, mosques and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zincirli-medrese">Zincirli Medrese</a> date from that era. In December 1917 it hosted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kurultai">Kurultai</a> that proclaimed the Crimean People's Republic. Nearby stands the cave monastery of the Dormition.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bakhchysarai.jpg" alt="Bakhchysarai" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Aleksander Kaasik · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Baht%C5%A1isarai-Khaani_palee_Krimmis.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
